        "matta, rug, carpet"
      ],
      "dcDescription": [
        "Mongolia Carpet with warp and support element of cotton. Most likely made in any of the North China border towns. Has either been used as a temple mat or a Mongol tent. Patterns with stylized flowers within a square frame. Original bottom color roast red with flowers and ornaments in blue, yellow and white. The same colors return in the stretcher. Frames and edges of blue wool. Acquired by dr. Montell in Beijing in 1932. Slightly damaged by moths and worn in the uncharted edges. 74 x 74 cm. [ocr] Knotted temple or tent mat. Cotton in warp and intermediate, wool in knots. Slightly smeared, espe"
